  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116294",
      "title": "The Starting Projects: Frontend & Backend",
      "lectureOrder": 219,
      "videoOrder": 210,
      "sourceHash": "7a052bc23618231c968b9adc5763bdc0aa490e3be4f6c32f1fcd2242f6c3b451",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 3.33,
          "en": "Now for this section, as always,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.33,
          "end": 6.93,
          "en": "you find a brand new starting project attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.93,
          "end": 9.96,
          "en": "And this attached project actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.96,
          "end": 13.353,
          "en": "is the combination of two projects, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.25,
          "end": 16.56,
          "en": "It's an Angular application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.56,
          "end": 19.08,
          "en": "but it's an Angular application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.08,
          "end": 23.28,
          "en": "that also has this backend folder inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.28,
          "end": 28.28,
          "en": "and that's now a folder that holds no Angular code at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.74,
          "end": 32.64,
          "en": "Instead, it's a totally separate kind of application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.64,
          "end": 37.47,
          "en": "which I simply included into this Angular application folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.47,
          "end": 39.42,
          "en": "for simplicity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.42,
          "end": 43.2,
          "en": "But you could move that backend folder out of this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.2,
          "end": 47.04,
          "en": "and run that backend somewhere else on your computer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.04,
          "end": 49.65,
          "en": "and you would still be able to work with it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.65,
          "end": 52.08,
          "en": "I just put it into this project folder here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.08,
          "end": 54.42,
          "en": "to keep these files together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.42,
          "end": 57.33,
          "en": "Because this backend folder now contains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.33,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "a very simple Node Express application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 64.59,
          "en": "which has nothing to do with Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.59,
          "end": 68.91,
          "en": "and it's in the end a simple API, a simple web API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.91,
          "end": 71.76,
          "en": "that's included in this app.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.76,
          "end": 75.84,
          "en": "that accepts get requests to various paths,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.84,
          "end": 78.99,
          "en": "to various routes, and also some other requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.99,
          "end": 80.78999999999999,
          "en": "like put and delete,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.78999999999999,
          "end": 85.78999999999999,
          "en": "which we can use to store data here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.49,
          "end": 88.2,
          "en": "Now in this dummy application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.2,
          "end": 91.5,
          "en": "I do have some JSON files prepared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.5,
          "end": 95.00999999999999,
          "en": "that contains some data, at least one of them does,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.00999999999999,
          "end": 98.82,
          "en": "and will therefore still operate on some dummy data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.82,
          "end": 102.42,
          "en": "but now dummy data that's not part of the Angular app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.42,
          "end": 106.59,
          "en": "but instead of the backend to simulate a scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.59,
          "end": 110.223,
          "en": "where we have a real backend we might be talking to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.24000000000001,
          "end": 113.28,
          "en": "I am also not using a database here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 115.59,
          "en": "but instead these files for storing data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.59,
          "end": 117.27000000000001,
          "en": "But in the end, the result of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.27000000000001,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "is the same because a database in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 122.76,
          "en": "is also just data stored in files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.76,
          "end": 124.98,
          "en": "just of course in a more efficient way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.98,
          "end": 127.02,
          "en": "But to keep things simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.02,
          "end": 130.44,
          "en": "this backend will simply store and access data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.44,
          "end": 132.33,
          "en": "in these JSON files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.33,
          "end": 134.91,
          "en": "But the main idea is the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.91,
          "end": 137.57999999999998,
          "en": "that we manage that data in a backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.57999999999998,
          "end": 141.18,
          "en": "and not in the Angular application itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.18,
          "end": 143.49,
          "en": "Instead, in this section, you will learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.49,
          "end": 147,
          "en": "how to reach out to that backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147,
          "end": 150.03300000000002,
          "en": "from inside your Angular application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.65,
          "end": 153.63,
          "en": "Therefore, what you should do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.63,
          "end": 155.88,
          "en": "after you downloaded this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.88,
          "end": 158.67000000000002,
          "en": "is you should of course run npm install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.67000000000002,
          "end": 159.96,
          "en": "as you always should,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.96,
          "end": 162.993,
          "en": "to install all these Angular dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.1,
          "end": 165.21,
          "en": "But once that's done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 168.3,
          "en": "you should also navigate into that backend folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.3,
          "end": 172.5,
          "en": "in your terminal, and also run npm install there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.5,
          "end": 176.25,
          "en": "to also install the dependencies of the backend project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.25,
          "end": 179.85,
          "en": "Because again, it essentially is a separate project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.85,
          "end": 181.623,
          "en": "with its own dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.3,
          "end": 187.23,
          "en": "And then still navigate it into that backend folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.23,
          "end": 188.97,
          "en": "in your terminal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.97,
          "end": 193.97,
          "en": "you should run npm start to start that backend Web API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.64,
          "end": 197.43,
          "en": "and you should keep that process up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.43,
          "end": 200.04,
          "en": "Otherwise, you'll not be able to connect to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.04,
          "end": 201.633,
          "en": "from your Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.56,
          "end": 205.74,
          "en": "Though you can stop at any time by pressing Ctrl + C",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.74,
          "end": 207.27,
          "en": "if you need to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.27,
          "end": 210.6,
          "en": "Then you should just restart it by running npm start again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.6,
          "end": 213.543,
          "en": "if you wanna work on this application again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 214.68,
          "end": 217.29,
          "en": "And now in a separate terminal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.29,
          "end": 220.82999999999998,
          "en": "in a separate tab or a totally new terminal window,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.82999999999998,
          "end": 225.03,
          "en": "you should go into your main project folder again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 225.03,
          "end": 227.97,
          "en": "so not into the backend folder, but the main project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 227.97,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "And there also run npm start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 232.68,
          "en": "to start that Angular application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.68,
          "end": 234.993,
          "en": "that Angular development server again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.16,
          "end": 237.96,
          "en": "And once you did that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.96,
          "end": 241.5,
          "en": "you should see a page like this on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 241.5,
          "end": 244.98,
          "en": "if you visit localhost:4200,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.98,
          "end": 247.95,
          "en": "and that's now the application we'll work on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.95,
          "end": 249.54,
          "en": "And we'll for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 249.54,
          "end": 252.75,
          "en": "start by making sure that we populate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 252.75,
          "end": 255.6,
          "en": "this available places box here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 255.6,
          "end": 259.08,
          "en": "with some data that should indeed be fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 259.08,
          "end": 260.85,
          "en": "from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.85,
          "end": 264.27,
          "en": "And therefore the question is how do we connect Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 264.27,
          "end": 267.75,
          "en": "to that backend and how do we get access to the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 267.75,
          "end": 270.09,
          "en": "that's stored in those files there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 270.09,
          "end": 273.9,
          "en": "so that's stored in that database there, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 273.9,
          "end": 276.36,
          "en": "even though it's technically not a real database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 276.36,
          "end": 278.67,
          "en": "but it works in the same way here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.67,
          "end": 280.803,
          "en": "how do we get access to that?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
